      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The hamlet grew when the Harlem Railroad arrived in 1852, shipping cattle, hay, and milk to New York City.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/craryville_new_york",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Craryville Train Station opened in 1905 as part of the New York Central extension to Chatham, serving passengers until 1972 and freight until 1980.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/craryville_new_york",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Early settlement of Craryville dates back to the late 18th century as part of Livingston Manor, a 1686 land grant.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9,
